From: emerald port
Subject: [PATCH] emerald: declare sweet_vtimer_intid under defined(SWEET)

0017 defined the variable and sleh.c use under #if defined(SWEET), but the
protos.h extern used #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) only. EMERALD
sets ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_EMERALD and #define SWEET 1 (0082 EMERALD.h), so
sleh.c saw an undeclared identifier on DEVELOPMENT^ARM64^EMERALD.

Align the extern guard with pe_fiq.c / sleh.c. SWEET is only #define'd by
SWEET.h / EMERALD.h - not by VMAPPLE/T810x/etc. board configs.

Proven CI failure (run 39378467932):
  osfmk/arm64/sleh.c:1870:15: error: use of undeclared identifier 'sweet_vtimer_intid'

---
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm/protos.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm/protos.h
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@
 int uart_getc(void);
 
 void pe_init_fiq(void);
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(SWEET)
 extern uint32_t sweet_vtimer_intid;
 #endif

